<title>GERMANY: VW signs deal on air conditioner compressor.</title>
<headline>VW signs deal on air conditioner compressor.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG said on Friday it will team up with a German company to develop and build about 500,000 air conditioner compressors after production begins in 1999.</p>
<p>VW said the deal with Wankel Rotary of Korb, Germany, calls for the parts to be built at a VW plant in Salzgitter and used in vehicle production to meet growing demand for air conditioning systems.</p>
<p>The carmaker said about 80 million marks would be invested into the project, which will also create 100 new jobs.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
